WEBVTT

1
00:00:50.634 --> 00:00:52.051
Aagghh!

2
00:01:01.603 --> 00:01:03.312
Whoo!

3
00:01:05.441 --> 00:01:09.402
Here comes a big one! Come on.
You got to try this.

4
00:01:09.486 --> 00:01:13.072
- Will you just stop it?
- Why? What's wrong?

5
00:01:13.157 --> 00:01:15.950
- We're in a whale. Don't you get it?
- A whale?

6
00:01:16.034 --> 00:01:19.996
A whale! 'Cause you had to ask for
help. And now we're stuck here.

7
00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:24.333
- A whale? You know, I speak whale.
- You're insane. You can't speak whale.

8
00:01:24.418 --> 00:01:27.253
I have to get out. I
have to find my son.

9
00:01:28.255 --> 00:01:33.009
I have to tell him how
old sea turtles are!

10
00:01:44.021 --> 00:01:45.021
Hey.

11
00:01:47.399 --> 00:01:48.941
You okay?

12
00:01:55.657 --> 00:01:57.241
There, there.

13
00:01:57.326 --> 00:01:59.952
It's all right. It'll be okay.

14
00:02:00.037 --> 00:02:02.497
No. It won't.

15
00:02:02.581 --> 00:02:04.874
Sure it will. You'll see.

16
00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:09.545
No. I promised him I'd never
let anything happen to him.

17
00:02:11.173 --> 00:02:14.884
Huh. That's a funny
thing to promise.

18
00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:15.968
What?

19
00:02:16.053 --> 00:02:18.554
You can't never let
anything happen to him.

20
00:02:18.639 --> 00:02:21.224
Then nothing would
ever happen to him.

21
00:02:23.852 --> 00:02:26.062
Not much fun for little Harpo.

22
00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:39.200
- What's going on?
- Don't know. I'll ask him.

23
00:02:40.536 --> 00:02:44.664
- What's...
- Dory.

24
00:02:44.748 --> 00:02:46.207
Going

25
00:02:46.291 --> 00:02:48.417
on?

26
00:02:54.132 --> 00:02:57.301
- I think he says we've stopped.
- Of course we've stopped.

27
00:02:57.386 --> 00:03:01.097
Stop trying to speak whale. You're
going to make things worse.

28
00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:02.181
What is that noise?

29
00:03:06.603 --> 00:03:08.479
Oh, no. Look what you did.

30
00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:13.442
The water's going down.
It's going down!

31
00:03:17.447 --> 00:03:20.700
- Really? You sure about that?
- Look. Already it's half-empty.

32
00:03:21.159 --> 00:03:24.787
- Hmm. I'd say it's half-full.
- Stop that. It's half-empty!

33
00:03:28.083 --> 00:03:30.626
Okay, that one was
a little tougher.

34
00:03:30.711 --> 00:03:33.629
He either said we should go
to the back of the throat

35
00:03:33.714 --> 00:03:35.881
or he wants a root beer float.

36
00:03:35.966 --> 00:03:39.677
Of course he wants us to go
there. That's eating us!

37
00:03:39.761 --> 00:03:42.471
How do I taste, Moby?
Do I taste good?

38
00:03:42.556 --> 00:03:44.640
Tell him I'm not
interested in being lunch.

39
00:03:44.725 --> 00:03:47.143
- Okay. He's...
- Stop talking to him.

40
00:03:53.567 --> 00:03:56.611
- What is going on?
- I'll check. What...

41
00:03:56.695 --> 00:03:59.322
No. No more whale. You
can't speak whale.

42
00:03:59.406 --> 00:04:00.990
Yes, I can.

43
00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:02.074
No, you can't.

44
00:04:02.159 --> 00:04:05.661
You think you can do these
things, but you can't, Nemo.

45
00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:12.501
- Okay.
- Dory!

46
00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:19.342
He says it's time to let go.

47
00:04:19.426 --> 00:04:21.719
Everything's going
to be all right.

48
00:04:21.803 --> 00:04:23.763
How do you know?

49
00:04:23.847 --> 00:04:26.182
How do you know something
bad isn't going to happen?

50
00:04:26.892 --> 00:04:28.100
I don't!

51
00:04:41.698 --> 00:04:43.491
Aaaggghhh!

52
00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:53.459
We're alive!

53
00:04:55.212 --> 00:04:57.254
Look. Syd-ney.

54
00:04:57.339 --> 00:04:59.298
Sydney! Sydney.

55
00:04:59.383 --> 00:05:00.883
Sydney again.

56
00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:04.220
You were right. We made it!

57
00:05:04.888 --> 00:05:06.972
We're going to find my son.

58
00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:14.063
Thank you, Sir.

59
00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:16.190
Wow. I wish I could speak whale.

60
00:05:16.274 --> 00:05:18.484
Now we find the
boat that took him.

61
00:05:18.568 --> 00:05:21.362
- Right.
- Come on. We can do this!

62
00:05:37.379 --> 00:05:39.672
Morning. It's morning, everyone.

63
00:05:39.756 --> 00:05:44.427
Today's the day. The sun is shining, the
tank is clean and we are getting out of...

64
00:05:44.511 --> 00:05:45.761
The tank is clean.

65
00:05:46.763 --> 00:05:48.472
The tank is clean!

66
00:05:49.599 --> 00:05:50.766
But how?

67
00:05:50.851 --> 00:05:53.811
Boss must have installed
it while we were sleeping.

68
00:05:53.895 --> 00:05:56.397
- What are we going to do?
- What's it say, Peach?

69
00:05:57.774 --> 00:05:59.525
I can't hear you, Peach.

70
00:05:59.609 --> 00:06:03.946
The Aqua Scum 2003 is an all-purpose,
self-cleaning salt-water purifier

71
00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:06.615
that extends the life
of your aquarium fish.

72
00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:07.783
Stop it!

73
00:06:07.868 --> 00:06:11.746
The Aqua Scum is programmed to
scan your tank every five minutes?

74
00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:13.539
Scan? What does that mean?

75
00:06:18.879 --> 00:06:21.630
Temperature
82 degrees, pH balance normal.

76
00:06:21.882 --> 00:06:23.007
Oooh!

77
00:06:23.091 --> 00:06:24.133
Nice.

78
00:06:25.677 --> 00:06:28.888
Curse you, Aqua Scum!

79
00:06:28.972 --> 00:06:32.308
- That's it for the escape plan.
Then what are we going to do about...

80
00:06:32.934 --> 00:06:34.268
Darla!

81
00:06:34.352 --> 00:06:36.145
Stay down, kid.

82
00:06:38.482 --> 00:06:41.066
- False alarm. - My nerves
can't take much more.

83
00:06:41.318 --> 00:06:43.903
What are we going to
do when that brat gets here?

84
00:06:43.987 --> 00:06:46.655
- I'm thinking, I'm thinking.
- Help!

85
00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:48.657
- Help me!
- Hold on. I'm coming.

86
00:06:48.784 --> 00:06:49.825
Help me!

87
00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:52.745
Swim down! Come on, kid.
Swim down!

88
00:06:52.829 --> 00:06:55.206
- Everybody jump in.
- Swim down!

89
00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:56.749
What the...

90
00:06:57.751 --> 00:06:58.834
Good work.

91
00:06:59.377 --> 00:07:01.670
- Gill!
- Sharkbait!

92
00:07:03.215 --> 00:07:06.342
- Roll, kid! Lean, kid! Roll!
- Go to the window.

93
00:07:10.889 --> 00:07:13.224
Whoops! That would
have been a nasty fall.

94
00:07:13.308 --> 00:07:16.268
- I don't want to go belly-up!
- Calm down, Nemo.

95
00:07:16.353 --> 00:07:18.604
You won't go belly-up.
I promise.

96
00:07:18.688 --> 00:07:19.688
You're going to be okay.

97
00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:24.944
Darla!

98
00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:32.576
Do any of these boats
look familiar to you?

99
00:07:32.661 --> 00:07:34.870
No, but the boat has to be here.

100
00:07:34.955 --> 00:07:37.998
- We're going to find it.
- I'm totally excited.

101
00:07:38.083 --> 00:07:40.626
- Are you excited?
- Dory, wake up. Come on.

102
00:07:41.628 --> 00:07:42.670
Duck!

103
00:07:43.797 --> 00:07:46.340
That's not a duck.
It's a pelican!

104
00:07:55.725 --> 00:07:58.561
No! I didn't come this
far to be breakfast.

105
00:08:06.653 --> 00:08:09.071
Hey, Nigel. Would
you look at that?

106
00:08:09.155 --> 00:08:10.155
What?

107
00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:13.534
Sun's barely up and Gerald's
had more than he can handle.

108
00:08:13.618 --> 00:08:16.787
Yeah. Reckon somebody ought
to help the poor guy.

109
00:08:18.582 --> 00:08:21.375
Well, don't everybody
fly off at once!

110
00:08:24.546 --> 00:08:26.547
All right, Gerald. What is it?

111
00:08:26.631 --> 00:08:28.424
Fish got your tongue?

112
00:08:28.925 --> 00:08:30.384
Love a duck!

113
00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:32.136
I've got to find my son Nemo.

114
00:08:32.846 --> 00:08:33.888
Nemo?

115
00:08:33.972 --> 00:08:37.892
He's that fish that's been
fighting the whole ocean.

116
00:08:37.976 --> 00:08:40.311
Hey, I know where your son...

117
00:08:41.605 --> 00:08:43.689
Wait. Come back.

118
00:08:43.773 --> 00:08:46.275
- Stop!
- Keep going. He's crazy.

119
00:08:46.359 --> 00:08:48.652
I've got something to tell you.

120
00:08:52.616 --> 00:08:53.657
Mine.

121
00:08:58.246 --> 00:09:01.957
Okay. Don't make
any sudden moves.

122
00:09:02.042 --> 00:09:05.586
Hop inside my mouth
if you want to live.

123
00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:09.798
Hop into your mouth? And how
does that make me live?

124
00:09:09.883 --> 00:09:14.053
- Mine? - Because I can
take you to your son.

125
00:09:14.137 --> 00:09:15.471
Yeah, right!

126
00:09:15.555 --> 00:09:19.934
No. I know your son. He's orange.
He's got a gimpy fin on one side.

127
00:09:20.018 --> 00:09:22.311
- That's Nemo!
- Mine! Mine! Mine!

128
00:09:25.148 --> 00:09:27.399
Fasten your seat belts!

129
00:09:28.234 --> 00:09:30.694
Mine! Mine! Mine!

130
00:09:33.615 --> 00:09:35.532
Whoo-hoo!

131
00:09:49.381 --> 00:09:51.340
Everybody hold on!

132
00:09:55.011 --> 00:09:57.221
Mine! Mine! Mine!

133
00:10:04.104 --> 00:10:05.938
- Too loud. Too loud for me.

134
00:10:06.022 --> 00:10:08.232
Twinkle, twinkle,
little star

135
00:10:08.316 --> 00:10:11.068
Find a happy place.
Find a happy place!

136
00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:14.363
Darla, your
uncle will see you now.

137
00:10:16.199 --> 00:10:19.034
All right. Let's see
those Pearly whites.

138
00:10:19.577 --> 00:10:21.120
I'm a piranha.

139
00:10:21.204 --> 00:10:22.788
They're in the Amazon.

140
00:10:22.872 --> 00:10:26.375
And a piranha's a fish.
Just like your present.

141
00:10:28.211 --> 00:10:29.795
- I got a fishy!
- Oh, no.

142
00:10:31.047 --> 00:10:32.339
Poor little guy.

143
00:10:32.424 --> 00:10:34.258
- He's dead.
- Sharkbait!

144
00:10:34.342 --> 00:10:36.010
Yay! Fishy, fishy, fishy!

145
00:10:36.094 --> 00:10:39.930
Must have left your present in the
car, sweetie. I'll go and get it.

146
00:10:40.015 --> 00:10:41.515
He's still alive!

147
00:10:41.599 --> 00:10:43.267
Why is he playing dead?

148
00:10:43.351 --> 00:10:45.102
He's going to get flushed
down the toilet.

149
00:10:45.186 --> 00:10:47.646
He's going to get out of here.

150
00:10:47.731 --> 00:10:51.650
- What a smart little guy.
- No, not the trash can!

151
00:10:52.902 --> 00:10:54.945
Hey! I found his dad.

152
00:10:55.030 --> 00:10:56.613
- Where's Nemo?
- Dentist!

153
00:10:56.698 --> 00:10:58.407
- He's over there.
- What's a dentist?

154
00:10:59.701 --> 00:11:02.077
- Get in there.
- I can't go in there.

155
00:11:02.162 --> 00:11:05.581
Oh, yes you can. Charge!

156
00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:08.417
- What the...

157
00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:12.379
Darla, sweetie, look out.

158
00:11:16.009 --> 00:11:19.011
Hold still. Easy, easy.

159
00:11:20.555 --> 00:11:21.889
Hold still!

160
00:11:21.973 --> 00:11:23.766
It's all right. Nobody's
going to hurt you.

161
00:11:32.150 --> 00:11:33.859
Nemo.

162
00:11:33.943 --> 00:11:35.944
- Oh, my goodness.
- Gotcha!

163
00:11:37.322 --> 00:11:39.490
- Nemo!
- Daddy?

164
00:11:40.325 --> 00:11:42.951
Out with you.
And stay out!

165
00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:46.288
- Daddy?
- Fishy?

166
00:11:47.123 --> 00:11:48.207
Fishy!

167
00:11:48.291 --> 00:11:50.000
Wake up! Wake up!

168
00:11:50.085 --> 00:11:51.543
- Oh, no!
- To the top

169
00:11:51.628 --> 00:11:53.212
of Mount Wannahockaloogie.

170
00:11:53.296 --> 00:11:55.589
Why are you sleeping?

171
00:11:55.840 --> 00:11:58.050
- Hurry!
- Bloat!

172
00:12:01.262 --> 00:12:03.138
Ring of Fire!

173
00:12:05.141 --> 00:12:06.475
Fishy!

174
00:12:08.728 --> 00:12:10.395
- Get it out!
- Crikey!

175
00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:12.147
The animals have gone mad!

176
00:12:14.067 --> 00:12:16.235
Get it out!

177
00:12:16.319 --> 00:12:18.278
- Smack her in the head!
- Go, Gill, go!

178
00:12:18.363 --> 00:12:20.322
There's a fish in my hair!

179
00:12:21.157 --> 00:12:23.158
- Gill.
- Sharkbait.

180
00:12:23.243 --> 00:12:26.120
Tell your dad I said hi.

181
00:12:30.375 --> 00:12:31.416
Aaggh!

182
00:12:31.501 --> 00:12:33.293
- Go get him.

183
00:12:37.841 --> 00:12:39.299
He did it!

184
00:12:40.176 --> 00:12:42.261
- I'm happy.
- Is he going to be okay?

185
00:12:42.345 --> 00:12:45.139
Don't worry. All drains
lead to the ocean.

186
00:12:45.223 --> 00:12:46.682
Fishy!

187
00:12:49.144 --> 00:12:50.310
Aaggh!

188
00:12:54.649 --> 00:12:56.191
Daddy!

189
00:13:32.562 --> 00:13:34.605
I'm... I'm so sorry.

190
00:13:36.316 --> 00:13:37.858
Truly I am.

191
00:13:56.002 --> 00:13:57.502
- Hey...
- Dory.

192
00:13:58.755 --> 00:14:02.591
If it wasn't for you, I never
would have even made it here.

193
00:14:03.509 --> 00:14:04.968
So thank you.

194
00:14:07.180 --> 00:14:08.680
Hey, wait a minute.

195
00:14:09.098 --> 00:14:11.516
Wait. Where are you going?

196
00:14:11.601 --> 00:14:14.478
It's over, Dory.
We were too late.

197
00:14:16.105 --> 00:14:17.981
Nemo's gone.

198
00:14:18.066 --> 00:14:19.983
I'm going home now.

199
00:14:20.068 --> 00:14:22.152
No. No, you can't.

200
00:14:24.113 --> 00:14:25.280
Stop!

201
00:14:28.243 --> 00:14:30.494
Please don't go away. Please?

202
00:14:31.913 --> 00:14:33.956
No one's ever stuck with
me for so long before.

203
00:14:34.624 --> 00:14:36.875
And if you leave...

204
00:14:37.669 --> 00:14:40.462
I remember things
better with you. Look.

205
00:14:40.546 --> 00:14:42.798
P. Sherman, 42...

206
00:14:43.841 --> 00:14:45.550
42...

207
00:14:45.969 --> 00:14:49.263
Bah! I remember it. It's there.
I know it is.

208
00:14:49.347 --> 00:14:51.932
Because when I look at
you, I can feel it.

209
00:14:52.016 --> 00:14:54.351
And I look at you and I...

210
00:14:55.979 --> 00:14:57.437
I'm home.

211
00:15:00.108 --> 00:15:03.318
Please. I don't want
that to go away.

212
00:15:04.404 --> 00:15:06.321
I don't want to forget.

213
00:15:07.865 --> 00:15:09.908
I'm sorry, Dory,

214
00:15:09.993 --> 00:15:11.493
but I do.

215
00:15:23.381 --> 00:15:26.717
- Manna from heaven.
- Sweet nectar of life.

216
00:15:27.343 --> 00:15:28.969
Hey!

217
00:15:29.053 --> 00:15:32.014
- This is our spot.
- Go on. Get out of here.

218
00:15:33.266 --> 00:15:35.851
Hey, hey, hey.

219
00:15:35.935 --> 00:15:37.602
Yeah, that's it.

220
00:15:38.771 --> 00:15:40.522
Too right, mate!

221
00:15:40.606 --> 00:15:42.232
I got a live one here!

222
00:15:42.317 --> 00:15:44.776
- Have you seen my dad?
- Gotcha!

223
00:15:44.861 --> 00:15:47.446
- Come back here.
- You let him go!

224
00:15:49.574 --> 00:15:50.574
Dad!

225
00:15:55.955 --> 00:15:57.289
No!

226
00:16:10.219 --> 00:16:12.346
- Excuse me.
- No.

227
00:16:12.430 --> 00:16:14.848
- Are you all right?
- I don't know where I am.

228
00:16:14.932 --> 00:16:17.351
I don't know what's going on.
I think I lost somebody,

229
00:16:17.435 --> 00:16:19.144
but I can't remember.

230
00:16:19.228 --> 00:16:21.646
- It's okay.
- I can't remember.

231
00:16:21.731 --> 00:16:25.359
I'm looking for someone, too.
We can look together.

232
00:16:26.903 --> 00:16:28.862
- I'm Dory.
- I'm Nemo.

233
00:16:28.946 --> 00:16:30.405
Nemo?

234
00:16:31.074 --> 00:16:32.324
That's a nice name.

235
00:16:41.626 --> 00:16:43.460
- Dad!
- Dad!

236
00:16:43.544 --> 00:16:45.128
- Dad.
- Dad.

237
00:16:45.213 --> 00:16:46.814
Wait a minute. Is it
your dad or my dad?

238
00:16:46.881 --> 00:16:48.006
My dad.

239
00:16:48.091 --> 00:16:50.008
- Got it. Dad!
- Where are we anyway?

240
00:16:50.093 --> 00:16:51.301
Dad!

241
00:16:52.136 --> 00:16:54.471
Syl... Schai...

242
00:16:54.555 --> 00:16:55.972
Sydney.

243
00:16:56.057 --> 00:16:58.642
P. Sherman, 42
Wallaby Way, Sydney.

244
00:17:00.436 --> 00:17:01.853
- Nemo!
- What?

245
00:17:01.938 --> 00:17:03.563
It's you! Nemo!

246
00:17:03.648 --> 00:17:05.273
Yes. I'm Nemo.

247
00:17:05.358 --> 00:17:08.110
You're Nemo. You were dead.
I saw you.

248
00:17:08.194 --> 00:17:10.529
And then... Here you are.
You're not dead.

249
00:17:10.613 --> 00:17:13.031
And your father... Your father!

250
00:17:13.116 --> 00:17:16.034
My father? You know my father?
Where is he?

251
00:17:16.119 --> 00:17:17.869
He went this way. Quick!

252
00:17:19.497 --> 00:17:20.539
Hey!

253
00:17:20.623 --> 00:17:22.624
Have you seen an
orange fish swim by?

254
00:17:22.708 --> 00:17:24.709
- It looks like him.
- But bigger.

255
00:17:24.794 --> 00:17:27.504
I saw him, but I'm not
telling you where he went.

256
00:17:27.588 --> 00:17:31.049
And there's no way
you're going to make me.

257
00:17:33.594 --> 00:17:34.761
Mine.

258
00:17:34.846 --> 00:17:37.180
All right. I'll talk!

259
00:17:37.265 --> 00:17:39.808
He went to the fishing grounds.

260
00:17:44.772 --> 00:17:46.440
- Hey, look out.
- Sorry.

261
00:17:46.524 --> 00:17:48.316
I'm just trying to get home.

262
00:17:51.654 --> 00:17:53.071
Daddy!

263
00:17:53.156 --> 00:17:55.907
- Nemo?
- Daddy!

264
00:17:55.992 --> 00:17:57.075
Nemo?

265
00:17:57.160 --> 00:17:58.994
Dad! Nemo's alive!

266
00:17:59.078 --> 00:18:00.328
Dory?

267
00:18:00.413 --> 00:18:02.205
- Nemo!
- Daddy!

268
00:18:02.290 --> 00:18:05.667
- Nemo! I'm coming, Nemo!
- Dad!

269
00:18:05.751 --> 00:18:08.295
Nemo! Thank goodness.

270
00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:11.214
It's all right, son.
It's going to be okay.

271
00:18:11.632 --> 00:18:14.009
Turn around! You're
going the wrong way.

272
00:18:16.888 --> 00:18:19.431
- Aaggh! Look out!
- Move!

273
00:18:41.037 --> 00:18:42.537
- Dory!
- Come on.

274
00:18:44.123 --> 00:18:46.291
Help! Get us out!

275
00:18:47.043 --> 00:18:49.377
No, no, no! Dory!

276
00:18:49.462 --> 00:18:51.630
- Dad, I know what to do.
- Nemo, no!

277
00:18:51.714 --> 00:18:54.466
We have to tell all the
fish to swim down together.

278
00:18:54.550 --> 00:18:56.801
- Get out of there.
- This will work.

279
00:18:56.886 --> 00:18:59.179
No, I am not going
to lose you again.

280
00:18:59.263 --> 00:19:02.641
There's no time. It's the
only way we can save Dory.

281
00:19:04.185 --> 00:19:05.393
I can do this!

282
00:19:07.188 --> 00:19:10.565
You're right. I know you can.

283
00:19:10.942 --> 00:19:13.985
- Lucky fin.
- Now, go. Hurry!

284
00:19:14.070 --> 00:19:16.363
Tell all the fish to swim down.

285
00:19:16.781 --> 00:19:19.741
Well, you heard my son. Come on.

286
00:19:21.577 --> 00:19:25.830
- Dory, you have to tell everybody to...
- Swim down together.

287
00:19:25.915 --> 00:19:28.124
Do you understand
what I'm saying?

288
00:19:28.209 --> 00:19:30.001
Swim down!

289
00:19:34.423 --> 00:19:38.176
- Everybody swim down. - Come
on. You have to swim down.

290
00:19:38.261 --> 00:19:40.929
Down! Swim down!

291
00:19:43.140 --> 00:19:46.643
Swim down! Swim down!

292
00:19:54.610 --> 00:19:56.820
Don't give up! Keep swimming!

293
00:19:57.947 --> 00:19:59.781
Just keep swimming!

294
00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:05.120
That's it!

295
00:20:08.708 --> 00:20:10.041
It's working!

296
00:20:12.878 --> 00:20:16.006
Keep swimming!

297
00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:18.633
Just keep swimming!

298
00:20:18.718 --> 00:20:20.927
- Come on, Dad!
- You're doing great, son.

299
00:20:21.012 --> 00:20:23.346
- That's my dad.
- Let's get to the bottom.

300
00:20:24.473 --> 00:20:26.641
Just keep swimming

301
00:20:26.726 --> 00:20:28.852
Almost there.
Keep swimming!

302
00:20:32.481 --> 00:20:37.193
Keep swimming!

303
00:20:48.664 --> 00:20:49.748
Hey!

304
00:20:49.832 --> 00:20:51.333
Where's Nemo?

305
00:20:51.709 --> 00:20:52.792
There!

306
00:20:55.463 --> 00:20:57.339
Oh, no. Nemo!

307
00:21:04.347 --> 00:21:08.266
Nemo?

308
00:21:10.019 --> 00:21:13.021
It's okay. Daddy's here.
Daddy's got you.

309
00:21:18.319 --> 00:21:20.695
- Daddy?
- Oh, thank goodness.

310
00:21:20.780 --> 00:21:22.530
Daddy...

311
00:21:22.615 --> 00:21:25.367
- I don't hate you.
- Oh, no, no, no.

312
00:21:26.494 --> 00:21:28.870
I'm so sorry, Nemo.

313
00:21:38.422 --> 00:21:40.632
Hey, guess what?

314
00:21:40.716 --> 00:21:43.093
- What?
- Sea turtles...

315
00:21:43.177 --> 00:21:45.053
I met one.

316
00:21:45.137 --> 00:21:48.932
And he was 150 years old.

317
00:21:49.016 --> 00:21:50.975
150?

318
00:21:51.060 --> 00:21:52.560
Yep.

319
00:21:53.229 --> 00:21:57.315
'Cause Sandy Plankton said
they only lived to be 100.

320
00:21:58.275 --> 00:21:59.734
Sandy Plankton?

321
00:21:59.819 --> 00:22:03.655
Think I would cross the ocean and
not know as much as Sandy Plankton?

322
00:22:03.739 --> 00:22:06.491
He was 150! Not 100.

323
00:22:06.575 --> 00:22:09.911
Who is this Sandy Plankton
that knows everything wrong?

324
00:22:12.248 --> 00:22:15.583
Time for school! Time for
school! Get up! Let's go!

325
00:22:16.544 --> 00:22:19.379
- I'm going to win.
- No, you're not.

326
00:22:19.463 --> 00:22:23.007
- I did it.
- My own son beats me.

327
00:22:23.092 --> 00:22:25.135
Climb aboard, explorers.

328
00:22:25.219 --> 00:22:28.513
So then the sea cucumber looks
over at the mollusk and says,

329
00:22:28.597 --> 00:22:31.099
"With fronds like these,
who needs anemones?"

330
00:22:33.352 --> 00:22:35.145
Well, hello, Nemo. Who's this?

331
00:22:35.229 --> 00:22:38.565
- Exchange student.
- I'm from the EAC, dude.

332
00:22:38.649 --> 00:22:40.942
- Sweet.
- Totally.

333
00:22:41.861 --> 00:22:45.572
Seriously, Marty, did you really
do all the things you say you did?

334
00:22:45.656 --> 00:22:46.948
Pardon me.

335
00:22:47.825 --> 00:22:48.908
Hello.

336
00:22:50.453 --> 00:22:51.995
Don't be alarmed.

337
00:22:52.079 --> 00:22:55.206
We wanted to make sure our
newest member got home safely.

338
00:22:55.291 --> 00:22:57.375
- Thanks.
- We'll see you next week.

339
00:22:57.460 --> 00:23:01.004
- Keep up with the programme, Dory.
- Remember, fish are friends.

340
00:23:01.088 --> 00:23:03.423
Not food! Bye!

341
00:23:03.507 --> 00:23:05.383
Hold on. Here we go.

342
00:23:05.468 --> 00:23:07.177
Next stop, knowledge.

343
00:23:07.261 --> 00:23:09.721
Bye, son. Have fun.

344
00:23:09.805 --> 00:23:10.930
Bye, Dad.

345
00:23:11.974 --> 00:23:14.309
Oh! Mr. Ray, wait. I
forgot something.

346
00:23:19.482 --> 00:23:21.149
Love you, Dad.

347
00:23:22.359 --> 00:23:24.360
I love you, too, son.

348
00:23:27.156 --> 00:23:29.574
Uh, Dad? You can let go now.

349
00:23:29.658 --> 00:23:30.992
Sorry.

350
00:23:31.076 --> 00:23:33.203
Now go have an adventure.

351
00:23:33.287 --> 00:23:35.580
Goodbye. See you later, dudes!

352
00:23:35.664 --> 00:23:37.415
- Bye, Elmo.
- Nemo.

353
00:23:37.500 --> 00:23:41.002
- Nemo. Bye, Nemo.
- See you after school, Dory.

354
00:23:41.879 --> 00:23:43.171
Bye, Dad!

355
00:23:44.673 --> 00:23:46.174
Bye, son.

356
00:24:03.856 --> 00:24:05.336
Barbara.
Mmm-hmm?

357
00:24:05.361 --> 00:24:06.820
I don't understand it.

358
00:24:06.904 --> 00:24:10.198
Here this thing has a lifetime
guarantee and it breaks.

359
00:24:10.282 --> 00:24:14.869
Had to clean the tank myself, take
the fish out, put 'em in bags and...

360
00:24:15.371 --> 00:24:17.205
Where'd the fish go?

361
00:24:22.670 --> 00:24:24.963
Come on, Peach!

362
00:24:25.047 --> 00:24:27.507
You got it. That's it.
You can do it.

363
00:24:27.591 --> 00:24:29.843
That's the shortest red
light I've ever seen.

364
00:24:29.927 --> 00:24:31.678
Come on, Peach.

365
00:24:41.564 --> 00:24:42.981
Now what?
